The application was successfully opened in the browser using:

```text
https://myapp.example.com
```

The frontend displayed:

```text
Welcome to Our Store
```

The backend was also accessible through:

```text
https://myapp.example.com/api
```

This confirmed that the complete Ingress and HTTPS setup works from the browser.

---

# 27. Kustomize

After the individual Kubernetes resources had been tested, Kustomize was used to manage the complete deployment.

The file:

```text
k8s/kustomization.yaml
```

contains:

```yaml
apiVersion: kustomize.config.k8s.io/v1beta1
kind: Kustomization

namespace: assignment1

resources:
  - namespace.yaml
  - frontend-config.yaml
  - backend-config-v2.yaml
  - secret.yaml
  - frontend-deployment.yaml
  - backend-deployment.yaml
  - mongodb-deployment.yaml
  - app-ingress.yaml
  - cluster-issuer.yaml
```

The old `backend-config.yaml` was removed from the Kustomization because the application now uses:

```text
backend-config-v2
```

---

# 28. Kustomize Validation

Before applying the complete configuration, the generated Kubernetes manifests were previewed:

```bash
kubectl kustomize k8s/
```

The output showed all expected resources.

The complete configuration was then deployed using:

```bash
kubectl apply -k k8s/
```

The result showed resources being created or reported as unchanged/configured.

This demonstrated that the entire application can now be managed using a single Kustomize command.

---

