# 30. Final Result

The project successfully demonstrates a Kubernetes application deployed on Minikube with:

* Kubernetes namespace isolation
* Frontend Deployment
* Backend Deployment
* MongoDB Deployment
* Kubernetes Services
* ConfigMaps
* Immutable ConfigMap versioning
* Kubernetes Secrets
* NGINX Ingress
* Ingress routing
* RBAC
* Ingress security configuration
* cert-manager
* Self-signed TLS certificate
* HTTP → HTTPS redirection
* HTTPS application access
* Kustomize-based deployment
* Browser verification

The final access path is:

```text
https://myapp.example.com
```

Frontend:

```text
https://myapp.example.com/
```

Backend:

```text
https://myapp.example.com/api
```

The complete Kubernetes configuration can be deployed with:

```bash
kubectl apply -k k8s/
```

The final architecture demonstrates how multiple application components can be deployed, secured, configured, exposed, and managed using Kubernetes on a local Minikube cluster.
